  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions`. Its `description` says when to use it in terms of the user's task: \"Use at the start of any work in a project that tracks requirements with Habeas\", followed by concrete project signals (a `habeas` dev-dependency, a `habeas.toml`, `{req}` directives, and references in code). It also names the other bundled skills (habeas-requirements, habeas-refactor, habeas-evidence, habeas-bootstrap-requirements) to pick for particular tasks. The requirement's MAY allows that. The description meets the MUST, and the site has no gap.",
